ng-top:12pt;padding-bottom:12pt;line-height:1.1500000000000001;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:center}.c15{padding-top:20pt;padding-bottom:4pt;line-height:1.1500000000000001;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left}.c18{padding-top:15pt;padding-bottom:8pt;line-height:1.1500000000000001;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left}.c7{font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:12pt;font-family:"Arial";font-style:normal}.c12{text-decoration-skip-ink:none;font-size:13.5pt;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;color:#681da8;text-decoration:underline}.c44{font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:"Arial";font-style:normal}.c21{text-decoration-skip-ink:none;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;color:#1155cc;text-decoration:underline}.c27{text-decoration-skip-ink:none;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;color:#681da8;text-decoration:underline}.c45{background-color:#ffffff;max-width:468pt;padding:72pt 72pt 72pt 72pt}.c53{margin-left:0.9pt;text-indent:-0.4pt}.c39{margin-left:216pt;text-indent:36pt}.c17{color:#000000;font-size:13pt}.c37{margin-left:144pt;text-indent:36pt}.c25{color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit}.c31{padding:0;margin:0}.c20{color:#1f1f1f}.c6{font-weight:700}.c47{color:#666666}.c40{font-size:12pt}.c50{text-indent:-36pt}.c35{height:12pt}.c38{font-size:13.5pt}.c49{page-break-after:avoid}.c43{margin-left:72pt}.c13{margin-left:36pt}.c54{font-size:13pt}.c4{color:#001d35}.title{padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;font-size:26pt;padding-bottom:3pt;font-family:"Arial";line-height:1.1500000000000001;page-break-after:avoid;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left}.subtitle{padding-top:0pt;color:#666666;font-size:15pt;padding-bottom:16pt;font-family:"Arial";line-height:1.1500000000000001;page-break-after:avoid;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left}li{color:#000000;font-size:12pt;font-family:"Arial"}p{margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:12pt;font-family:"Arial"}h1{padding-top:20pt;color:#000000;font-weight:700;font-size:16pt;padding-bottom:4pt;font-family:"Arial";line-height:1.1500000000000001;page-break-after:avoid;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left}h2{padding-top:18pt;color:#000000;font-size:16pt;padding-bottom:6pt;font-family:"Arial";line-height:1.1500000000000001;page-break-after:avoid;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left}h3{padding-top:16pt;color:#434343;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:4pt;font-family:"Arial";line-height:1.1500000000000001;page-break-after:avoid;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left}h4{padding-top:14pt;color:#666666;font-size:12pt;padding-bottom:4pt;font-family:"Arial";line-height:1.1500000000000001;page-break-after:avoid;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left}h5{padding-top:12pt;color:#666666;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:4pt;font-family:"Arial";line-height:1.1500000000000001;page-break-after:avoid;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left}h6{padding-top:12pt;color:#666666;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:4pt;font-family:"Arial";line-height:1.1500000000000001;page-break-after:avoid;font-style:italic;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left}</style></head><body class="c45 doc-content"><h1 class="c46" id="h.s1rgmqu3u84a"><span class="c6 c42">FINANCIAL CONFLICT OF INTEREST POLICY</span></h1><p class="c52 c49 c53 subtitle" id="h.er730dwgcqzo"><span class="c7 c47">Ronin Institute for Independent Scholarship 2.0 (RIIS 2.0)</span></p><p class="c41 subtitle" id="h.bizw64ekjq5l"><span class="c7 c47">California Nonprofit Public Benefit Corporation (Incorporated 2025)</span></p><p class="c52"><span class="c3">Approval Date: 2025-07-22 &bull; Effective Date: 2025-07-22 &bull; Version: 1.0 &bull; </span></p><p class="c52"><span class="c3">Approved by: Interim Council</span></p><p class="c29"><span class="c19 c6"></span></p><h1 class="c15" id="h.pzrj5dcvmdvy"><span class="c0">1. PURPOSE AND SCOPE</span></h1><p class="c2"><span class="c3">This policy establishes standards for identifying, managing, and reporting financial conflicts of interest (FCOI) to ensure the integrity of research, programs, and operations at the Ronin Institute for Independent Scholarship 2.0. This policy applies to all Investigators, key personnel, and employees involved in the design, conduct, or reporting of research or program activities.</span></p><p class="c2"><span>This policy is designed to comply with applicable federal regulations, including but not limited to the Public Health Service (PHS) Policy on Financial Conflict of Interest (42 CFR Part 50, Subpart F (see </span><span class="c21"><a class="c25" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-42/chapter-I/subchapter-D/part-50/subpart-F&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1759933447114788&amp;usg=AOvVaw00o1GieHdwGTQpuu7oYtdE">https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-42/chapter-I/subchapter-D/part-50/subpart-F</a></span><span class="c3">), and may be updated as necessary to meet specific funding agency requirements.</span></p><h1 class="c15" id="h.yd1iyziwwuky"><span class="c0">2. DEFINITIONS</span></h1><p class="c2"><span class="c6">Financial Conflict of Interest (FCOI)</span><span class="c3">: A significant financial interest that could directly and significantly affect the design, conduct, or reporting of research or other organizational activities.</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c6">Financial Interest</span><span class="c3">: Anything of monetary value received or held by an Investigator or their family members, including but not limited to:</span></p><ul class="c31 lst-kix_list_4-0 start"><li class="c33 c13 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Salary, consulting fees, honoraria, or other payments</span></li><li class="c13 c24 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Equity interests (stocks, stock options, or other ownership interests)</span></li><li class="c24 c13 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Intellectual property rights and interests</span></li><li class="c23 c13 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Travel reimbursements and expenses</span></li></ul><p class="c2"><span class="c6">Significant Financial Interest (SFI)</span><span class="c3">: A financial interest that meets one or more of the following criteria:</span></p><ul class="c31 lst-kix_list_14-0 start"><li class="c13 c33 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">For publicly traded entities: aggregate value exceeding $5,000 in the 12 months preceding disclosure</span></li><li class="c24 c13 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">For non-publicly traded entities: any amount of remuneration or equity interest</span></li><li class="c24 c13 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Intellectual property rights and interests upon receipt of income exceeding $5,000 in the 12 months preceding disclosure</span></li><li class="c13 c23 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Reimbursed or sponsored travel exceeding $5,000 in the 12 months preceding disclosure</span></li></ul><p class="c2"><span class="c6">Investigator</span><span class="c3">: Any individual responsible for the design, conduct, or reporting of research or other covered activities, including principal investigators, co-investigators, and other key personnel.</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c6">Family Members</span><span class="c3">: Spouse, domestic partner, and dependent children.</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c6">Institution</span><span class="c3">: Ronin Institute for Independent Scholarship 2.0 (AKA RIIS 2.0) and its subsidiaries or affiliates.</span></p><h1 class="c15" id="h.m2yjtnahbxex"><span class="c0">3. DISCLOSURE REQUIREMENTS</span></h1><h3 class="c1" id="h.d405j480wvt9"><span class="c11 c6">3.1 Annual Disclosure</span></h3><p class="c2 c13"><span class="c3">All Investigators must submit annual financial disclosure statements no later than the first business day on or after 15 April of each year, disclosing all significant financial interests held by themselves and their family members.</span></p><h3 class="c1" id="h.pyxywbu4a56"><span class="c11 c6">3.2 Ongoing Disclosure</span></h3><p class="c2 c13"><span class="c3">Investigators must update their disclosure within 30 days of:</span></p><ul class="c31 lst-kix_list_13-0 start"><li class="c28 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Acquiring new significant financial interests</span></li><li class="c22 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Changes to existing financial interests that create or alter potential conflicts</span></li><li class="c14 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Beginning new research projects or activities</span></li></ul><h3 class="c1" id="h.q4fd3kjnwy63"><span class="c11 c6">3.3 Travel Disclosure</span></h3><p class="c2 c13"><span class="c3">Investigators must disclose reimbursed or sponsored travel related to their institutional responsibilities, including:</span></p><ul class="c31 lst-kix_list_12-0 start"><li class="c28 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Purpose of trip</span></li><li class="c22 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Identity of sponsor/organizer</span></li><li class="c22 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Destination and duration</span></li><li class="c14 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Monetary value (if known)</span></li></ul><h3 class="c1" id="h.3o5ne8v0ydug"><span class="c11 c6">3.4 Disclosure Form</span></h3><p class="c2 c13"><span class="c3">All disclosures must be submitted using a form substantially similar to the RIIS 2.0 standard disclosure form template and include sufficient detail to enable conflict assessment. A template of the required form is appended to this policy as Appendix A</span></p><h1 class="c15" id="h.38x16bu4p23q"><span class="c0">4. REVIEW AND DETERMINATION PROCESS</span></h1><h3 class="c1" id="h.mzfen2ss1b53"><span class="c11 c6">4.1 Responsible Official</span></h3><p class="c2 c13"><span class="c3">The Council of RIIS 2.0 shall elect a person to serve as the Responsible Official of RIIS 2.0 for FCOI matters (AKA &ldquo;Responsible Official&rdquo;) by simple majority vote, and the Responsible Official may delegate review responsibilities to one or more qualified individuals or committees. In the case of a vacancy in the position of Responsible Official, the Secretary of RIIS 2.0 shall serve as interim Responsible Official.</span></p><h3 class="c1" id="h.drsxw1td5f1j"><span class="c11 c6">4.2 Review Timeline</span></h3><ul class="c31 lst-kix_list_2-0 start"><li class="c28 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Initial review of disclosures must be completed within 30 days of receipt</span></li><li class="c14 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Determinations regarding conflicts of interest must be made within 60 days of disclosure</span></li></ul><h3 class="c1" id="h.cgcd33xp23c1"><span class="c11 c6">4.3 Conflict Determination</span></h3><p class="c2 c13"><span class="c3">The Responsible Official will determine whether a significant financial interest constitutes a financial conflict of interest by assessing whether the interest could directly and significantly affect the design, conduct, or reporting of research or other institutional activities.</span></p><h3 class="c1" id="h.gt8mljyzjq0n"><span class="c11 c6">4.4 Documentation</span></h3><p class="c2 c13"><span class="c3">All reviews, determinations, and management decisions must be documented in writing and maintained in RIIS 2.0 records in a manner specified by the Secretary of RIIS 2.0.</span></p><h1 class="c15" id="h.7wv0ntevm5ac"><span class="c0">5. MANAGEMENT OF CONFLICTS</span></h1><h3 class="c1" id="h.akrngfma0lvz"><span class="c11 c6">5.1 Management Plan</span></h3><p class="c2 c13"><span class="c3">When a financial conflict of interest is identified, RIIS 2.0 will develop and implement a management plan before research or related activities commence. Management strategies may include:</span></p><ul class="c31 lst-kix_list_6-0 start"><li class="c28 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Disclosure of the conflict to relevant parties</span></li><li class="c22 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Monitoring of research or activities by independent reviewers</span></li><li class="c22 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Modification of the research plan or activities</span></li><li class="c22 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Disqualification from participation in affected activities</span></li><li class="c22 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Divestiture of significant financial interests</span></li><li class="c14 li-bullet-0"><span>Severance of relationships that create </span><span>financial</span><span class="c3">&nbsp;conflicts of interest</span></li></ul><h3 class="c1" id="h.dhfjqdnnyqyu"><span class="c11 c6">5.2 Monitoring and Compliance</span></h3><p class="c2 c13"><span class="c3">RIIS 2.0 will monitor compliance with management plans throughout the duration of relevant activities and conduct periodic reviews to ensure continued effectiveness.</span></p><h3 class="c1" id="h.loxtx62g5h7e"><span class="c11 c6">5.3 Failure to Comply</span></h3><p class="c2 c13"><span class="c3">Failure to comply with this policy may result in disciplinary action up to and including termination of affiliation, employment, or contract, and may require retrospective review of affected activities.</span></p><h1 class="c15" id="h.j5l4vpkrpnzf"><span class="c0">6. REPORTING REQUIREMENTS</span></h1><h3 class="c1" id="h.6w6enu5bgeva"><span class="c11 c6">6.1 External Reporting</span></h3><p class="c2 c13"><span class="c3">When required by funding agencies or regulations, RIIS 2.0 will submit FCOI reports within specified timeframes and update reports as circumstances change.</span></p><h3 class="c1" id="h.cfve6g3p320n"><span class="c11 c6">6.2 Public Accessibility</span></h3><p class="c2 c13"><span class="c3">When required by applicable regulations, RIIS 2.0 will make information about financial conflicts of interest publicly accessible through appropriate mechanisms.</span></p><h1 class="c15" id="h.tsj4hr8mi767"><span class="c0">7. TRAINING AND EDUCATION</span></h1><h3 class="c1" id="h.fsbvdwcp22xz"><span class="c11 c6">7.1 Required Training</span></h3><p class="c2 c13"><span class="c3">All Investigators must complete FCOI training:</span></p><ul class="c31 lst-kix_list_9-0 start"><li class="c28 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Prior to engaging in research or covered activities</span></li><li class="c22 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">At least every four years thereafter</span></li><li class="c22 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">When this policy is substantively updated</span></li><li class="c14 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">When an Investigator is found to be non-compliant</span></li></ul><h3 class="c1" id="h.uoo45zbgbe6l"><span class="c11 c6">7.2 Training Content</span></h3><p class="c2 c13"><span>Training will address this policy, applicable regulations, responsibilities for disclosure, and RIIS 2.0&#39;s review process. Absent training requirements determined by the Responsible Official to be more appropriate, the training content shall be as specified by the National Institutes of </span><span>Health</span><span>&nbsp;at </span><span class="c21"><a class="c25" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://grants.nih.gov/policy-and-compliance/policy-topics/fcoi/fcoi-training&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1759933447130357&amp;usg=AOvVaw3BLgoH82B-D0KFHg6rsFhW">https://grants.nih.gov/policy-and-compliance/policy-topics/fcoi/fcoi-training</a></span></p><h1 class="c15" id="h.r9a3hldleg8i"><span class="c0">8. RECORD RETENTION</span></h1><p class="c2"><span class="c40">RIIS 2.0 will maintain records related to financial conflicts of interest for at least </span><span>seven </span><span class="c3">years after final expenditure report submission or, for ongoing projects, until completion of the project, whichever is longer.</span></p><h1 class="c15" id="h.y4o6oslawyyl"><span class="c0">9. APPEALS PROCESS</span></h1><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Investigators may appeal conflict determinations or management decisions by submitting a written appeal to the Council within 30 days of notification. The appeal will be reviewed by individuals without conflicts of interest related to the matter.</span></p><h1 class="c15" id="h.atgccfd504hb"><span class="c0">10. INSTITUTIONAL CONFLICTS</span></h1><h3 class="c1" id="h.jd8ap6orbs95"><span class="c6 c11">10.1 Scope</span></h3><p class="c2 c13"><span class="c3">This policy also addresses institutional financial conflicts of interest that may arise from RIIS 2.0&#39;s own financial interests in research or other activities.</span></p><h3 class="c1" id="h.sazms6h1atp"><span class="c11 c6">10.2 Management</span></h3><p class="c2 c13"><span class="c3">Institutional conflicts will be managed through appropriate mechanisms, which may include independent oversight, disclosure, or other measures as determined by the Council.</span></p><h1 class="c15" id="h.l7le9jihb6h6"><span class="c0">11. POLICY ADMINISTRATION</span></h1><h3 class="c1" id="h.ex29qy41i454"><span class="c11 c6">11.1 Policy Updates</span></h3><p class="c2 c13"><span class="c3">This policy will be reviewed annually and updated as necessary to comply with applicable regulations and best practices.</span></p><h3 class="c1" id="h.6gd3nuqgz1py"><span class="c11 c6">11.2 Questions and Guidance</span></h3><p class="c2 c13"><span>Questions about this policy should be directed to a Council member or other designated Responsible Official at </span></p><h3 class="c1" id="h.oabcaben6ogv"><span class="c6 c17">11.3 Effective </span></h3><p class="c2 c13"><span class="c3">This policy is effective as of 2025-07-22 and supersedes all previous Financial Conflict of Interest policies.</span></p><h1 class="c49 c13 c55" id="h.pcfiaebh6ims"><span class="c0">12. Document history</span></h1><p class="c13 c34"><span class="c3">2025-09-19 Formatted - Rami Saydjari</span></p><p class="c34 c13"><span class="c3">2025-07-12 Revised - Rami Saydjari</span></p><p class="c34 c13"><span class="c3">2025-07-11 Revised - Rami Saydjari</span></p><p class="c34 c13"><span>2025-07-11 Created - Herbert J. Bernstein</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c6 c19">Council Approval<br></span></p><p class="c2 c35"><span class="c3"></span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Signed: ___________________________<br>Rami Saydjari, Secretary of RIIS 2.0</span><span style="overflow: hidden; display: inline-block; margin: 0.00px 0.00px; border: 0.00px solid #000000; transform: rotate(0.00rad) translateZ(0px); -webkit-transform: rotate(0.00rad) translateZ(0px); width: 200.50px; height: 82.14px;"><img alt="" src="https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXfXCXDPcRYb7_YVv0CwQP-cnC0E-fqGh73-abmFaQzdCje3qwTnk4_t3g5G0ZqFIj6m7bQ-gEG_IebFOJwWae8WNge-gmxi4DR-LXTYmU4zjtj2nyZIm7TqHlxqaNYTiGc?key=-ZUTtzKDFJP2qefC_a2VcQ" style="width: 200.50px; height: 82.14px; margin-left: 0.00px; margin-top: 0.00px; transform: rotate(0.00rad) translateZ(0px); -webkit-transform: rotate(0.00rad) translateZ(0px);" title=""></span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Date: 2025-07-22</span></p><p class="c2 c35"><span class="c3"></span></p><h1 class="c15 c49" id="h.2ce2ve2y23eh"><span class="c0">APPENDICES</span></h1><h2 class="c30" id="h.slk5ewv22p3v"><span class="c6">Appendix A:</span><span class="c26">&nbsp;Financial Disclosure Form Template</span></h2><p class="c16"><span class="c3">CONFIDENTIAL</span></p><p class="c16"><span class="c3">**This document is confidential and cannot be copied once completed**</span></p><p class="c16"><span class="c3">DRAFT 11 July 2025</span></p><p class="c16"><span class="c3">RONIN INSTITUTE FOR INDEPENDENT SCHOLARSHIP 2.0 DISCLOSURE STATEMENT </span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Name: ______________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Title of RIIS 2.0 Position or Affiliation: _______________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Sponsor of Proposal or Project, if any: _______________________________________&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Title of Proposal or Project, if any: __________________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span>Date of Application </span><span>of </span><span class="c3">this disclosure: ________________________________________&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class="c2 c35"><span class="c3"></span></p><p class="c2"><span>The purpose of this form is to promote transparency and objectivity in research by disclosing significant financial </span><span>interests</span><span>&nbsp;(SFI) of investigators and key project personnel. Disclosure may include conflicts for spouse and dependent children. This form applies to investigators and key project personnel</span><span>&nbsp;r</span><span>esearch scholars, project directors, principal investigators, and co-PIs, collaborators, consultants, post-docs, and graduate students who are responsible for the design, conduct, or reporting of research funded by the PHS, NSF, or other agencies with similar disclosure requirements. It can be used to satisfy the requirements of the Ronin Institute </span><span>Bylaws</span><span class="c3">&nbsp;Article 9 as well.</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Refer to RIIS 2.0 Financial Conflict of Interest Policy for more information.</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Reminder: Disclosure applies to information that reasonably appears to be related to the investigator&rsquo;s RIIS 2.0 responsibilities, including but not limited to any responsibilities that arise from RIIS 2.0 Fellowship or other affiliation or research activities conducted thereunder. </span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Please answer the following questions:</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">1. Publicly Traded-Entities - With regard to any publicly traded entity, a significant financial interest exists if you received any amount of remuneration from the entity in the twelve months preceding the disclosure and if there is value of any equity interest in the entity as of the date of disclosure. For purposes of this definition, remuneration includes salary and any payment for services not otherwise identified as salary (e.g., consulting fees, honoraria, paid authorship); equity interest includes any stock, stock option, or other ownership interest, as determined through reference to public prices or other reasonable measures of fair market value. Does not include mutual funds investments and retirement accounts, which the investigator does not control.</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Please provide information for investigators/self:</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Name of Organization &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Address&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Investment or Position&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Description</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">______________________________________________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">______________________________________________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">______________________________________________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">______________________________________________________________________&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">2. Privately Held Entities - With regard to any non-publicly traded entity, a significant financial interest exists if the value of any remuneration received from the entity in the twelve months preceding the disclosure or when the Investigator (or the Investigator&rsquo;s spouse and dependent children) holds any equity interest (e.g., stock, stock option, or other ownership interest).</span></p><p class="c2 c35"><span class="c3"></span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Please provide information for investigators/self, spouse, and dependent children:</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Identify Self, Spouse, Dependent Children&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Name of Organization&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Address&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class="c2 c39"><span class="c3">Investment or Position&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Description</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">______________________________________________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">______________________________________________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">______________________________________________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">______________________________________________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">3. List the name and describe the nature of any current employment or occupation of spouse or dependent children that is related to the area of research that is the subject of this application.</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Please separately list any such significant financial interest held by your spouse or your dependent children with any firm, corporation, association, partnership, or other organization that is involved in the area of research that is the subject of this application. </span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Identify Self, Spouse, Dependent Children&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Name of Organization&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Address&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class="c2 c39"><span class="c3">Investment or Position &nbsp;Description</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">______________________________________________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">______________________________________________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">______________________________________________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">______________________________________________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class="c2 c35"><span class="c3"></span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">4. Any reimbursement or sponsored travel paid by an entity, including non-profit organizations. Excludes travel sponsored by the Ronin Institute or reimbursed by a government agency, a U.S. institution of higher education, or a research institute affiliated with such, a medical center, or an academic teaching hospital. </span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Please provide information for investigators/self:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Organization Sponsoring Travel&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Purpose of Travel&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Destination&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class="c2 c37"><span class="c3">Duration of Travel (exact dates not necessary)</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">______________________________________________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">______________________________________________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">______________________________________________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">______________________________________________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">5. Identify income from intellectual property rights and interests (e.g. patents, copyrights). Excludes intellectual property rights assigned to the Ronin Institute and its royalties that flow to the investigator.</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">______________________________________________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">______________________________________________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">______________________________________________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">6. I agree:</span></p><ul class="c31 lst-kix_list_11-0 start"><li class="c33 c13 li-bullet-0"><span>To update this disclosure during the proposal award period or during the project, as new significant financial interests are obtained by me, my spouse or my dependent children. I will do this within thirty (30) days of acquiring or discovering such significant financial interest.</span></li><li class="c24 c13 li-bullet-0"><span>To cooperate in the development of a management plan, if needed.</span></li><li class="c23 c13 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">To comply with any conditions or restrictions imposed by the Ronin Institute to promote objectivity in research and manage, reduce, or eliminate actual or potential conflicts of interest.</span></li></ul><p class="c2 c35"><span class="c3"></span></p><p class="c2 c35"><span class="c3"></span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">________________________________________&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;_________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Signature&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Date</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c6 c54">Submission Process: </span></p><ul class="c31 lst-kix_uquwxtdwzdzf-0 start"><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c38 c4">Online Submission:<br></span><span class="c4 c38">Many institutions have moved to online submission portals, such as </span><span class="c12"><a class="c25" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.google.com/search?client%3Dsafari%26sca_esv%3Df186cf072ac0f3b9%26cs%3D0%26sxsrf%3DAE3TifPkSuG29DpGVcmrYuqNrQ-OlfUHbw%253A1752323086685%26q%3DIRBNet%26sa%3DX%26ved%3D2ahUKEwjvyuKYqLeOAxU7F1kFHfKAFa4QxccNegQIJxAB%26mstk%3DAUtExfAcfsvR-Xr_wUXfDPstvbmNfZRqU72N9tHR6pzDiV2z890C4KgDA8VuJgtq4Vh3XjeSEz3zRpI_OL7bGyo7SN5Hjh9wf2w2BnxS2X4XHNYW2EkrI8H0I9dgFCLBzpZJinQLHsdSGqWA3sIoW11F4Af74nkkV0JJEfpjzKHj4zWFh9svF81gNpFe2QdWrurNhaOyGor9Q9VALR9Q072-l2pphdfkRijIi12YiCbfzsLU5cXI7ojM2X4DfFzYQ4aujbSfabugh0xfinlBk5S1ik1X0MH8zVUPGpW5XkWMCcyE8w%26csui%3D3&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1759933447152551&amp;usg=AOvVaw1u3EQeCDAUPmTd1Fq2KPmR">IRBNet</a></span><span class="c38 c4">, </span><span class="c12"><a class="c25" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.google.com/search?client%3Dsafari%26sca_esv%3Df186cf072ac0f3b9%26cs%3D0%26sxsrf%3DAE3TifPkSuG29DpGVcmrYuqNrQ-OlfUHbw%253A1752323086685%26q%3DTOPAZ%26sa%3DX%26ved%3D2ahUKEwjvyuKYqLeOAxU7F1kFHfKAFa4QxccNegQIJxAC%26mstk%3DAUtExfAcfsvR-Xr_wUXfDPstvbmNfZRqU72N9tHR6pzDiV2z890C4KgDA8VuJgtq4Vh3XjeSEz3zRpI_OL7bGyo7SN5Hjh9wf2w2BnxS2X4XHNYW2EkrI8H0I9dgFCLBzpZJinQLHsdSGqWA3sIoW11F4Af74nkkV0JJEfpjzKHj4zWFh9svF81gNpFe2QdWrurNhaOyGor9Q9VALR9Q072-l2pphdfkRijIi12YiCbfzsLU5cXI7ojM2X4DfFzYQ4aujbSfabugh0xfinlBk5S1ik1X0MH8zVUPGpW5XkWMCcyE8w%26csui%3D3&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1759933447153421&amp;usg=AOvVaw09JTLI1qMxi2CvfNrHC2Z-">TOPAZ</a></span><span class="c38 c4">, or their own custom systems.</span></li><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c38 c4">Email Submission:<br></span><span class="c38 c4">Some institutions may still accept submissions via email, but it is crucial to follow their specific instructions regarding email addresses and required attachments.</span></li></ul><p class="c2 c35"><span class="c3"></span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c11 c6">Disposition of Review (By Responsible Official) </span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">I have reviewed the above information and the referenced proposal, and to the best of my knowledge, find no evidence of conflict of interest or the appearance thereof.</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OR</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">I have reviewed the above information and the referenced proposal, and to the best of my knowledge find that a significant financial interest requires a management plan and/or a possible conflict of interest or the appearance thereof. Details are attached. &nbsp;</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Therefore, circle as applicable:</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The PI and/or key/senior staff has been notified that s/he must resign from or relinquish the conflict prior to resuming work on the Project. </span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A management plan has been created to address the conflict that: &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class="c2 c13"><span class="c3">a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Describes role and duties of PI and/or senior/key personnel.</span></p><p class="c2 c43 c50"><span>b.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Sets forth how the management plan will safeguard the objectivity </span><span>of the</span><span class="c3">&nbsp;project performance and reporting.</span></p><p class="c2 c13"><span class="c3">c.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Sets forth how the management plan will be monitored.</span></p><p class="c2 c13"><span class="c3">d.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Provides other information as necessary. </span></p><p class="c2"><span>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The FCOI Policy h</span><span>as been accepted by the PI or senior/key personnel </span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;________________________________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Name of Responsible Official&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; ________________________________________&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;_________________</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Signature of Responsible Official&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Date</span></p><p class="c2"><span class="c3">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ronin Institute for Independent Scholarship 2.0</span></p><p class="c2 c35"><span class="c3"></span></p><h2 class="c30" id="h.i5eulefir2at"><span class="c6">Appendix B:</span><span class="c26">&nbsp;Management Plan Template</span></h2><p class="c51"><span class="c4">The </span><span class="c4">Financial Conflict of Interest (FCOI) management plan template outlines procedures to mitigate or eliminate conflicts of interest that may arise in research settings. It&#39;s a crucial document for ensuring objectivity and integrity in research, particularly when funded by federal agencies like </span><span class="c27"><a class="c25" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.google.com/search?client%3Dsafari%26cs%3D0%26sca_esv%3D0f8b8d0d41e4cc57%26sxsrf%3DAE3TifPJvEDICkt0X8koamrw4t40B9_LPQ%253A1752285831747%26q%3DNIH%26sa%3DX%26ved%3D2ahUKEwiJm5q0nbaOAxWyGFkFHdwgAJUQxccNegQIAhAB%26mstk%3DAUtExfB39_qXq9-H9QKhy4MtbSyqH4N1jJpOcHnXkIq7tQqaBLSTjpIgPIgQPwJEEYUwSr1nNT22iiRhQKEzCrwkffZx-0sDW6Y9nOAvFm6e3JLV80L7MYeIZnsZsELuQJy1uueKrGZGy_mgw5BbD8B216r7UXFRt50cHlyDWRlYLEyZupXLpAMTGuRBIvQrZkLaLwQ9V_jY_swT038f_rPWFVf90PhtCFGddl677I6689hsM4ygOPcxKG0wI95mJ5ggAvRVs-E8vlUNBL9WLEUX5OXc%26csui%3D3&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1759933447159558&amp;usg=AOvVaw1CfKULrkDOL58bBWDbLBMh">NIH</a></span><span class="c7 c4">.The plan details how to manage, reduce, or eliminate identified conflicts, focusing on safeguarding the research&#39;s objectivity. </span></p><p class="c18"><span class="c7 c4">Key Elements of an FCOI Management Plan Template:</span></p><ul class="c31 lst-kix_list_8-0 start"><li class="c5 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c4">Investigator Information:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Details of the investigator with the conflict, including name and role. </span></li></ul><p class="c32 c29 c13"><span class="c3"></span></p><ul class="c31 lst-kix_list_8-0"><li class="c5 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c4">Entity Information:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Name of the entity with which the investigator has a conflict. </span></li></ul><p class="c29 c13 c32"><span class="c3"></span></p><ul class="c31 lst-kix_list_8-0"><li class="c5 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c4">Nature of Conflict:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Description of the financial interest (e.g., consulting fees, equity, travel) and its value (or estimated value). </span></li></ul><p class="c32 c29 c13"><span class="c3"></span></p><ul class="c31 lst-kix_list_8-0"><li class="c5 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c4">Relationship to Research:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Explanation of how the financial interest relates to the research project and the basis for determining a conflict. </span></li></ul><p class="c32 c29 c13"><span class="c3"></span></p><ul class="c31 lst-kix_list_8-0"><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c4">Management Plan Components:</span></li></ul><ul class="c31 lst-kix_list_8-1 start"><li class="c10 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c4">Investigator&#39;s Role:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Description of the investigator&#39;s specific duties in the research. </span></li><li class="c10 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c4">Conditions:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Specific actions or restrictions imposed to manage the conflict. </span></li><li class="c10 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c4">Safeguarding Objectivity:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Explanation of how the plan will ensure objectivity in the research. </span></li><li class="c10 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c4">Agreement:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Confirmation that the investigator agrees to abide by the management plan. </span></li></ul><p class="c32 c29 c43"><span class="c3"></span></p><ul class="c31 lst-kix_list_8-0"><li class="c5 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c4">Monitoring and Reporting:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Procedures for monitoring the plan&#39;s effectiveness and reporting on its status. </span></li></ul><p class="c32 c29 c13"><span class="c3"></span></p><ul class="c31 lst-kix_list_8-0"><li class="c5 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c4">Annual Review:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Requirement for periodic review and potential updates to the plan. </span></li></ul><p class="c32 c29 c13"><span class="c3"></span></p><p class="c18"><span class="c7 c4">Examples of Management Strategies:</span></p><ul class="c31 lst-kix_list_3-0 start"><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c4">Public Disclosure:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Disclosing the conflict in publications, presentations, and to research participants.</span></li><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c4">Independent Review:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Appointing an independent reviewer to oversee the research.</span></li><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c4">Modifying the Research Plan:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Adjusting the research plan to minimize the conflict.</span></li><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c4">Personnel Changes:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Reassigning roles or removing the investigator from the conflicted area.</span></li><li class="c5 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c4">Reducing or Eliminating the Conflict:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;This could involve selling equity or ending the relationship causing the conflict. </span></li></ul><p class="c32 c29 c13"><span class="c3"></span></p><p class="c18"><span class="c7 c4">Importance of the Management Plan:</span></p><ul class="c31 lst-kix_list_5-0 start"><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c4">Compliance:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Meets </span><span class="c4">the </span><span class="c4">requirements of federal agencies like the </span><span class="c27"><a class="c25" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://grants.nih.gov/grants/policy/nihgps/html5/section_4/4.1.10_financial_conflict_of_interest.htm&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1759933447168303&amp;usg=AOvVaw2_nGQPVUM4ek54bWWg5KYf">NIH</a></span><span class="c4">.</span></li><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c4">Objectivity:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Ensures research remains unbiased and reliable.</span></li><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c4">Transparency:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Promotes openness and accountability in the research process.</span></li><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c6 c4">Public Trust:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Helps maintain public confidence in research findings</span></li></ul><h2 class="c30" id="h.qg4i1lacmora"><span class="c6">Appendix C:</span><span class="c26">&nbsp;Training Requirements Checklist</span></h2><p class="c2"><span class="c3">Depending on the source of support for the relevant activities, more stringent training may be required, but the minimum training required for all persons affiliated with RIIS 2.0 is the online training specified by the National Institutes of Health</span></p><h2 class="c30" id="h.4lt89i2ougf5"><span><br></span><span class="c6">Appendix D:</span><span class="c26">&nbsp;Relevant Federal Regulations Reference</span></h2><p class="c18"><span class="c7 c4">Federal regulations</span></p><p class="c9"><span class="c4">The primary federal regulation governing Financial Conflicts of Interest (FCOI) in research is </span><span class="c20">42 CFR Part 50 Subpart F</span><span class="c7 c4">, also known as the &quot;Promoting Objectivity in Research&quot; regulation. </span></p><p class="c9"><span class="c7 c4">This regulation establishes standards designed to ensure that the design, conduct, and reporting of research funded by the Public Health Service (PHS), which includes the National Institutes of Health (NIH), are free from bias due to an investigator&#39;s conflicting financial interests. </span></p><p class="c9"><span class="c7 c4">Key aspects of the PHS FCOI regulations include:</span></p><ul class="c31 lst-kix_list_1-0 start"><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c20">Disclosure of Financial Interests:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Investigators are required to disclose their significant financial interests related to their institutional responsibilities, including compensation from non-profit entities and sponsored travel.</span></li><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c20">Definition of Significant Financial Interest (SFI):</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;For PHS investigators, an SFI includes anything of monetary value over $5,000 received or held by the investigator, their spouse, or dependent children, that reasonably appears to be related to the investigator&#39;s institutional responsibilities.</span></li><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c20">Mandatory Training:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Investigators are required to complete FCOI training at least every four years, or sooner if policies change or non-compliance is identified.</span></li><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c20">Institutional Responsibility:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Institutions receiving PHS funding are responsible for implementing FCOI policies, reviewing investigator disclosures, determining whether FCOIs exist, and developing and implementing management plans to mitigate or eliminate conflicts.</span></li><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c20">Reporting Requirements:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Institutions are required to report FCOIs to the relevant PHS funding agency, including details about the investigator, the nature of the SFI, the value of the interest, how the interest relates to the research, and the management plan implemented.</span></li><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c20">Foreign Financial Interests:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Investigators must disclose all foreign financial interests (e.g., income from foreign entities, including foreign governments) exceeding a specific threshold ($5,000). </span></li></ul><p class="c9"><span class="c4">In addition, </span><span class="c20">18 U.S.C. &sect; 208</span><span class="c4">, the basic criminal conflict of interest statute, prohibits government employees from participating in official matters where they have a financial interest.</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="c18"><span class="c4 c7">California laws and regulations</span></p><p class="c9"><span class="c4">California has its own robust set of </span><span class="c4">conflict-of-interest</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;laws and regulations, primarily stemming from the </span><span class="c20">Political Reform Act (PRA)</span><span class="c7 c4">. These laws are grounded in the principle that government officials owe paramount loyalty to the public and should not allow personal or private financial considerations to influence their decision-making. </span></p><p class="c9"><span class="c7 c4">Key elements of California&#39;s FCOI framework include:</span></p><ul class="c31 lst-kix_list_10-0 start"><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c20">Disqualification from Decision-Making:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Public officials are prohibited from participating in governmental decisions if it&#39;s foreseeable that the decision will have a financial impact on their personal finances or other financial interests.</span></li><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c20">Definition of Financial Interest:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;The PRA defines various financial interests that can lead to a conflict, such as income or gifts exceeding certain thresholds, investments, and real property interests.</span></li><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c20">Disclosure Requirements:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Public officials are required to disclose their financial interests on a Statement of Economic Interests (Form 700) to ensure transparency and accountability.</span></li><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c20">Conflict of Interest Codes:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;State and local agencies must adopt and regularly update conflict of interest codes that identify designated positions requiring disclosure and specify the types of financial interests that must be reported.</span></li><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c20">Disqualification Procedures:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Specific procedures exist for officials to disqualify themselves from decisions where a conflict exists, including publicly identifying the conflict and leaving the room during discussions.</span></li><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c20">Exceptions:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;Certain exceptions to the conflict of interest rules may apply, such as the &quot;public generally&quot; exception or situations where an official is legally required to participate.</span></li><li class="c8 li-bullet-0"><span class="c20">Enforcement:</span><span class="c4">&nbsp;The Fair Political Practices Commission (FPPC) is responsible for enforcing the Political Reform Act and related conflict of interest rules. </span></li></ul><p class="c9"><span class="c7 c4">In the context of research, some California regulations specifically address FCOI. For example, the California Code of Regulations, Title 17, Section 100003, outlines conflict of interest rules for non-ICOC members of the Scientific and Medical Research Funding Working Group, including disclosure requirements for certain financial interests related to grant applications. </span></p><p class="c2 c35"><span class="c3"></span></p><p class="c2 c35"><span class="c3"></span></p></body></html>